00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.170
It's called the Golden Windows.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.530
And it goes a little something like this.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.800
There was a little girl named Sue

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.400
who lived with her family in a big brown building in the city.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.730
From her window, she could see a faraway building

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.890
that during the day looked like any other.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.840
But every night, Sue waited for the sunset

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.520
when the building's windows turned to gold and diamonds.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:04:59.970
And Sue wished...

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.480
that she lived in a building as wonderful as that.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.020
One day, she set off down the street to see the windows up close.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.220
But when she got there, the windows she saw were made of ordinary glass.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.020
Just then, a little girl came out of the building.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.040
Sue asked her if she knew where the wonderful building

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.900
with windows of gold and diamonds had gone.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.200
The little girl smiled, for she knew the building well.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.740
She turned Sue around just as the sun was setting

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.960
and pointed to a building far away.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.510
with shimmering glimmering windows when Sue saw it she gasped for the building

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:42.150
she was looking at was hers and so as night fell Sue happily hurried home to

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:47.510
her own beautiful building with windows of golden diamonds and the lucky family

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:52.910
that lived there so in the end Sue realized that both buildings were pretty

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.630
it was just how you looked at them you know what looking at your stars I think

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.690
they're both pretty too

